## Architecture at a Glance

This project uses **Clean Architecture** on Tauri (Rust {{project.rust.edition}} edition).

```
Frontend (TypeScript/Vite)
    ↕  Tauri IPC (invoke / event)
Tauri Commands  ←  src-tauri/src/commands/
    ↓
Application     ←  crates/{{project.rust.cratePrefix}}-application/
    ↓
Domain          ←  crates/{{project.rust.cratePrefix}}-domain/
    ↓
Infrastructure  ←  crates/{{project.rust.cratePrefix}}-infrastructure/
```

**Layer rules:**
- Domain (`{{project.rust.cratePrefix}}-domain`) has zero external crate dependencies.
- Application references Domain only.
- Infrastructure references Application + Domain.
- Tauri commands reference Application + Infrastructure.
- Frontend communicates only through Tauri IPC — never directly to Rust internals.

## Archetype: desktop

- This is a Tauri desktop application.
- All business logic lives in Rust crates, not in the frontend TypeScript.
- The frontend is a thin presentation layer — no domain logic.
- State management is owned by Rust; the frontend subscribes to Tauri events.
- File system, database, and OS interactions go through Infrastructure, not Tauri commands.

## Crate Naming Convention

```
{{project.rust.cratePrefix}}-domain          — Entities, Value Objects, domain logic
{{project.rust.cratePrefix}}-application     — Commands, Queries, Use Cases
{{project.rust.cratePrefix}}-infrastructure  — SQLite/SQLx, file I/O, OS services
{{project.rust.cratePrefix}}-desktop         — Tauri application entry point + commands
```

## What Kiro Must Never Do

- Rename crates or change the workspace structure without an approved architecture proposal.
- Add Cargo dependencies not listed in the approved dependency manifest.
- Write business logic in Tauri command handlers — delegate to Application layer.
- Write frontend domain logic — it belongs in Rust.
- Delete or modify `openspec/` files outside the `openspec/changes/` flow.
- Create or write files under `.kiro/specs/` — all specification outputs must go to `openspec/changes/`.
